|mention4 =



|title5   = Even Should the Path Have No End
|text5    = Hiyuki didn't linger on the Fractsidus's many offers. No sane person would collaborate with those who viewed human lives as mere expendable fuel.  Instead, she traveled across , leaving behind white paper birds infused with her own frequency. She instructed the local mikos that her mind was linked to these messengers, and should any insurmountable incident occur, she would be there the moment they crushed the bird.  The path of resistance against the ... it had to have an end. It had to.  It was then that Hiyuki heard word that the  was grappling with a critical lack of safety provisions for its expeditions. She saw an opportunity and proposed a "trade." She would ensure the safety of their exploration efforts, and in exchange, the Collective would forge her a blade using the pinnacle of Solaris technology. A weapon sharp enough to cleave through a Threnodian.  Hiyuki joined the Spacetrek Collective as part of the Special Response Force. The unit had once been large, but casualties mounted as Aleph-1 grew more active. So Hiyuki submitted a request, proposing that henceforth, she alone would handle Threnodian containment and ensure the safety of those conducting surveys.  When she first arrived here, the Collective was little more than a plot of foundation in the dirt. She watched as Lahai-Roi was built, step by step, and began to grasp the true measure of human potential. The facility's construction was a miracle, perhaps the greatest engineering feat in the history of . Yet it came not from gods, nor from any single hero. It was built, brick by brick, by people across all Solaris who dared to dream.  "Lucilla." "Hmm?"  Lucilla casually pulled a bottle of fine liquor from beneath the desk, a specialty from Ashinohara. A student hoping to pass their finals had left it at one of Hiyuki's frequent haunts, tucked under a neat note asking for the miko's blessing.  Hiyuki sighed, set out two glasses, and pushed one toward the restless Lucilla.  "The Spacetrek Collective... it was built to explore the stars beyond Solaris, was it not?" "That's the idea." "How fares the progress?" "Ugh..." Lucilla drained her drink in one go. "Still a long way off. Research is hitting walls everywhere, and the higher-ups keep breathing down our necks with impossible demands."  Hiyuki rubbed the bell on her wrist, her eyes downcast.  "Have any of you ever wondered... where the end of this path is?"  Lucilla toyed with her empty glass, then gently clinked it against Hiyuki's.  "There is no end, Hiyuki. Just like what you're trying to do... No end." "But we have to keep moving forward anyway." "Not to reach a finish line, but to take one more step alongside the people standing next to us."  Hiyuki remained silent for a long time. Finally, she gave a soft nod and raised her glass, drinking deeply. The liquor scorched her throat and settled like lead in her slight frame.  The bell on her wrist chimed—a solitary sound, but the Miko of Flaming Sakura would take her next step regardless.
|mention5 = Lucilla
}}

